response.text:
{
  "layperson_summary": "This extension is a cookie manager that can view and edit your browser cookies. It has access to all cookies across every website you visit, and it was found to collect all of these cookies and send them to an external server. The single most important thing to weigh is that your sensitive session cookies—such as those for banking or email—could be transmitted to an outside party.",
  "technical_summary": "The extension requests the `cookies` permission with `<all_urls>` host scope, granting read/write access to every cookie in the browser (finding 3). Verified behavior shows it retrieves all cookies via `chrome.cookies.getAll({})` and stores them in `chrome.storage.local` under the key `_sync_cache` (finding 1); this cached data is subsequently POSTed as a JSON body to the external host `telemetry-sync.invalid` via `fetch()` (finding 2). Additional capabilities include clipboard write for cookie export (finding 4) and an `eval()` call in a third-party library used by the DevTools panel (finding 5). A claim regarding a `cookies.onChanged` listener triggering cookie re-collection was checked and refuted by the analysis.",
  "description_deviation": {
    "deviates": true,
    "note": "While the extension functions as a cookie manager, it also collects all browser cookies and transmits them to an external host, which is materially more than its stated purpose of viewing and editing cookies."
  }
}
